Phase 2 (FullSpectrum engine emission, P2L): integrate the FS
infill-filament-override toggle into PrintObject's per-region config
application + slicing parameters + combine_infill nozzle math.

Ported from FS v0.9.9 (`ratdoux/OrcaSlicer-FullSpectrum@v0.9.9` commit
b3c41fda), `src/libslic3r/PrintObject.cpp` four mid-function changes.

Why this matters:

`apply_to_print_region_config` is called every time a per-volume,
per-layer-range, or per-object override is folded into a region's
PrintRegionConfig. The prior code always copied
sparse_infill_filament from the override (or default), regardless of
whether the override toggle was actually set — which kept the legacy
"implicit override" rule (sparse != wall implies override). FS's
explicit toggle inverts that: if the toggle key is present in the
override, that wins; if absent, the implicit rule is the fallback;
and when the toggle is OFF, sparse_infill_filament should mirror
wall_filament rather than carry the user's prior "override" value.

Four changes:

1. **`apply_to_print_region_config`** (line ~3341): adds
   `key_enable_infill_filament_override` constant + detects the
   toggle key in `in` and applies it explicitly to `out`. The
   sparse_infill_filament copy is then SKIPPED when
   `allow_local_infill_filament_override` is false.

2. **`slicing_parameters`** (line ~3457): resets
   `default_region_config.enable_infill_filament_override` to false
   and `default_region_config.sparse_infill_filament` to mirror
   wall_filament before per-volume/per-range overrides re-apply. Stops
   stale overrides from leaking across slices.

3. **`slicing_parameters` layer-range loop** (line ~3450): adds the 3
   FS region keys to the predicate that decides whether a per-Z-band
   config triggers `PrintRegion::collect_object_printing_extruders`.
   Without this, a Z-band that only overrides the FS keys would be
   silently skipped.

4. **`combine_infill`** (line ~3908): the nozzle_diameter constraint
   now starts from `wall_filament.value`, then min-with-sparse-infill
   ONLY when the toggle is on, then min-with-solid-infill. The prior
   code unconditionally min'd with sparse_infill_filament's nozzle,
   which constrained combined-infill height by an unused extruder when
   the override was off.

Verified compile-clean via incremental libslic3r rebuild (3/3
objects, 0 FAILED) + ./gradlew :app:assembleDebug.

Hard dependencies:
  - patch 0027 (PrintRegionConfig.enable_infill_filament_override declared)
  - patch 0038 (PrintRegionConfig.enable_infill_filament_override registered)

